{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/471439-flash-backs-or-start-2371-bce","id":471439,"title":"Flash backs or start 2371 BCE?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-07T12:23:50-07:00","id":471439,"title":"Flash backs or start 2371 BCE?","content":"I'm new to Mummy, I've had the core book for ages and I've only really gotten around to really reading it after skimming through it a few times. Sothis Ascends looks like quite an interesting book and got me thinking about running a Mummy game. Based on a number of threads, I understand that I'll be best served by also getting the other supplements but I was curious if people were planning on using Sothis Ascends as a starting point or as a useful tool for flashbacks?<br /> <br /> Also as a new Mummy ST, is there any suggestions or tips for running a story through the ages?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3955-roguewind","name":"Roguewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T12:28:27-07:00","id":471477,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the idea of running the first session during the First Turn and taking advantage of Memory 1 to teach everyone the basics seems like an awesome idea. I'd make it a flashback, to get the players used to the mechanics and setting (maybe even set it as the last of their Sekhem dwindles), then flash-forwarding to your desired setting and running it from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:05:06-07:00","id":471727,"title":"","content":"Well, I just deleted everything I typed by accident.<br /> <br /> Basically, I wouldn't use the first Turn to introduce players to the game. <b>Mummy</b> deals a lot with Memory and remembering all the horrendous shit you've done over the years but, in Turn One, you haven't had any opportunity to do that yet. The game's major themes are diluted or filtered through a different perspective.<br /> <br /> Using it as a flashback is a good idea, though, but it's harder than you might think to say to a bunch of players new to the game, &quot;Okay, you wake up with new Purpose, no relics, no cult, no tomb, no Guild, and no Utterances. You're at Memory 1. Good luck.&quot; With experienced <b>Mummy</b> players that's great, but not for new ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:18:09-07:00","id":471731,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no, the First Turn is not a nice era-It's actively described as Hard Mode for Deathless players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T22:20:44-07:00","id":472208,"title":"","content":"I'd do it Memento-style - present to past. And I wouldn't just use the Sothic Turns - there are many more interesting time periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:36:39-07:00","id":473096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/471439-flash-backs-or-start-2371-bce?p=471727#post471727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I wouldn't use the first Turn to introduce players to the game. <b>Mummy</b> deals a lot with Memory and remembering all the horrendous shit you've done over the years but, in Turn One, you haven't had any opportunity to do that yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very good point that hadn't occurred to me. Think the plan will be go modern or at least a later period that gives me some time to slot all their 'forgotten' 